## Why This Is Asked
Explores practical RT-level data governance in OTCA: retention, holds, residency, and auditability across regions.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant policy store; region-scoped purges
- Data tagging: retention_version, tombstones
- Holds vs purge: immutable logs, legal holds
- Storage: object-lock Parquet; Kafka retention
- Testing: synthetic holds, burst scenarios, cross-region audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple eligibility check for purge
function eligibleForPurge(record, policy, currentDate) {
  const byTenant = policy.tenant_id === record.tenant_id;
  const byRegion = policy.region === record.region;
  const ageDays = (currentDate - new Date(record.createdAt)) / (1000*60*60*24);
  const notOnHold = !record.hold_id || !policy.hold_ids.includes(record.hold_id);
  return byTenant && byRegion && ageDays > policy.retention_days && notOnHold;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit deletion correctness across millions of records?
- How would you handle privacy-rights requests that require immediate data erasure despite holds?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes governance architecture across OTCA, focusing on immutability, auditability, regional residency, and rollback semantics in policy updates.

## Key Concepts
- Region residency and local sinks
- Versioned, immutable policy logs
- Global reconciler with audit trail
- Rollback and cross-region consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
function isNewVersion(current, incoming) {
  const toNum = s => (s||'0').split('.').map(n => parseInt(n,10));
  const [a,b,c] = toNum(current);
  const [x,y,z] = toNum(incoming);
  if (x !== a) return x > a;
  if (y !== b) return y > b;
  return (z||0) > (c||0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross-region rollback without downtime?
- How would you enforce strict write-once semantics across cloud storages?

## Why This Is Asked
This explores cost-aware telemetry and basic privacy controls in a common API stack.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic per-tenant sampling
- Privacy: IP redaction
- Streaming: SDK -> Pub/Sub
- Storage: Parquet/BigQuery regional
- Testing: volume control, privacy, dashboard freshness

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldSample(tenantId, eventId, rate) {
  const seed = `${tenantId}-${eventId}`;
  let h = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) h = (h * 31 + seed.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0;
  return (h % 100) < rate;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle dynamic rate changes per tenant at runtime?
- What if a tenant exceeds their quota; how would you implement backpressure?

